contentText:
Stove God Cooks insinuated that he may or may not be on this mythical album JAY-Z is supposedly making.

In a clip that&#8217;s been floating around rap social media circles, the Syracuse MC stopped by The Joe Budden Podcast recently and revealed that he sent Jigga a hook to use however and whenever he wants to.

&#8220;I sent Hov a hook. Don&#8217;t let me get on this album. I&#8217;m really gonna dance on you n&#8212;as. Now we gonna talk,&#8221; he proclaimed, before making sure he mentioned that he has no clue if a new album is coming or not. &#8220;I&#8217;m not confirming that big homie got an album coming out, but big homie, if you got an album coming out, use that hook I sent you. You know I was talking on that verse. Let&#8217;s do that.&#8221;

He added that he doesn&#8217;t want any money or percentage points for his contribution to whatever Jay has cooking; all he wants is a Roc-A-Fella chain. &#8220;I don&#8217;t want nothing. Keep everything,&#8221; he said. &#8220;Just send a Roc chain. I don&#8217;t want no percentage. Just send a Roc chain.&#8221;

Stove has been dealing with his own issues when it comes to albums. Fans have been clamoring for his sophomore project since he dropped the Roc Marciano -produced classing Reasonable Drought back in 2020 and had a show-stealing hook on &#8220;F.I.C.O.&#8221; off the Grammy-winning Clipse album .

However, after many pump fakes and back-and-forths with his current label Babygrande, however, it looks like they&#8217;ve finally hashed things out and found common ground because he posted that they renegotiated a new deal on his Instagram Stories earlier this week. &#8220;I salute real sh&#8211;, always,&#8221; he wrote. &#8220;Respect to Chuck [Wilson] at Babygrande. He came and sat down face-to-face and we got the renegotiation done! Album on the way.&#8221;

As far as a new JAY-Z album is concerned, though? Roc Nation deaded those rumors earlier this month, calling the unsubstantiated claims &#8220;fake news&#8221; on the company&#8217;s IG Stories.
